# The median seconds each nested smoke row takes, one `<row> <seconds>` line
# per measured row. scripts/validate reads it: a diff-scoped run leaves out a
# row over its bound, smoke_bound_secs, which --full and the batch run on
# main still run. A row with no line counts as fast and runs.
#
# Measured on cachy on 2026-10-29 from emitted qml-smoke: row-secs lines
# in main tmp/main-run/unit+qml/{20261029T081048Z,20261029T101142Z,
# 20261029T113400Z,20261029T125818Z}/qml.log. Only 081048Z completed
# every row; 101142Z and 113400Z ended early, and 125818Z was still running.
# Completed-row samples from these partial runs are included. Keep only
# rows.list members, so nested jarvis-bubble and leak-plant timings are
# excluded. Medians round to whole seconds, halves up, for this format.
# Snapshot hashes, sample counts and exact medians:
# tmp/vgs-2049-measurement.json (VGS-2049 evidence artifact).
# These row costs are inclusive of nested calls and are not additive wall
# time when a row is called inside another row.
#
# Jarvis producer/control costs: one native final selection on cachy,
# 2026-10-29, vgs-2051-final-validation.service; measured row-secs 0/272
# in tmp/validation-VGS-2051.log. VGS-2051 approves these lane samples.
# Source validation is reused after this data-only cost refresh.
#
# Refresh: take the `qml-smoke: row-secs row=<row> secs=<seconds>` lines
# that scripts/smoke/harness.sh prints for each row, from the qml.log of the
# batch runs under the main checkout's tmp/main-run/, keep the rows
# scripts/smoke/rows.list names, and write each row's median over those
# runs, in the order of rows.list.
